sequenceDiagram
  %% tasks.sync of a task copy on the Gateway engine: the steps of task/sync.mmd (workflow operation-task-sync-copy, child task-copy-base) as executor primitives on the copy's Node. ADR 0267 and ADR 0271, implemented by TaskSyncEngineFlow: steps `fetch` (`instance.fetch_branch`), `sync` (`instance.sync_base`), `clear` and the failure step `clear_after_failure` (`instance.clear_base`). Runtime proof on a nested fleet is outstanding.
  %% Same contract as the Swamp run (docs/reference/tasks.md#bring-main-into-a-copy): fetch the default branch into the copy's Node mirror, import only the missing objects, move only refs/remotes/origin/<default>. Nothing is merged or rebased; the credential never enters the copy.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: task:sync
  %% kind: tasks.sync
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane EN icon=workflow pill=engine tone=purple
  %% lane N icon=server pill=executor tone=amber
  %% lane C icon=server pill=copy tone=green
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=origin tone=gray
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant EN as Engine<br/>Gateway and NATS
  participant N as Instance Node<br/>executor
  participant C as Task copy<br/>via executor
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>origin
  CLI->>GW: task:sync 42<br/>refresh the refs
  Note over GW: Admit the sync<br/>group 42 · capture the intent
  %%> Same admission as task/sync.mmd: an open external group with its own running task copy (`tasks.instance_not_running`), no unended copy turn (`tasks.copy_turn_unended`), and the group lock: no check or publish runs beside it
  %%> The intent pins the repository, the default branch, `task-42`, the copy's Instance, its Node mirror `/var/lib/orbit/instance-repositories/<instance>.git` and its start commit
  alt the engine admits the whole Operation
    %%> Admission, one decision per Operation (EngineKinds::routes):
    %%> - `tasks.sync` is in `ORBIT_ENGINE_KINDS`
    %%> - the copy's Node reports `instance.fetch_branch`, `instance.sync_base` and `instance.clear_base` in `$KV.NODES`, and the feature `instance.fetch_seed`
    %%> - the copy, its runtime, its branch, its mirrors and its published and approved commits match the flow's shape and the group's own copy on that Node; a Project that reads with the Gateway's GitHub CLI login runs on Swamp
    %%> - the flow accepts the plan shape; a part it does not cover throws `EngineUnsupported` before any order
    %%> - eligible plan: a task copy (`copy` in the intent); a group without one keeps `tasks.no_workspace`
    Note over GW: Bind steps, take the lock<br/>commit, publish the start
    %%> - the copy's Instance lock is the Operation's from its admission; the step rows commit before the start event, from the pinned intent alone; an Operation never moves between engines after this
    %%> - the group stays fenced by its running Operation and the copy by the Instance lock: no removal or other writer of the copy starts until the sync ends
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
    EN->>N: Fetch the default branch<br/>instance.fetch_branch · mirror
    %%> Reuses `instance.fetch_branch` with the default branch: routing mints the one-hour read token (`contents: read`) once per Operation, keeps it encrypted in the Gateway cache for the journal's replay window or until the Operation ends, and sends the same blob to this Node only on every resend
    %%> The credential is written root-only beside the mirror in a file of this fetch's own for the Git calls and removed after them, whatever they did; a sibling fetch keeps its own file. It never reaches argv, the copy or a receipt
    %%> Desired state: the mirror holds `refs/heads/<default>` at origin's head; a repeat fetches nothing new. A missing mirror is made bare from the default's mirror (`seed`) in a scratch repository that takes the mirror's name only when complete, as the Swamp base phase makes it; with no default's mirror the fetch refuses
    N->>GH: Fetch the default head<br/>HTTPS · credential on the Node
    GH-->>N: Default head objects
    N-->>EN: Mirror head<br/>output: commit
    %%> `instance.fetch_branch` answers `commit: null` as success when origin lacks the branch (a create starts from the seed then); for a sync that is a failure: a null commit fails the Operation as `tasks.default_branch_missing`, and no old mirror head is ever imported
    EN->>C: Import missing objects<br/>bundle · remote ref only
    %%> Input: the non-null mirror head that the fetch receipt returned, pinned in the step input, so a resend imports the same commit even when origin moved
    %%> On the Node: takes the copy's `origin/<default>` and `task-42` commits, keeps as prerequisites only those the mirror also holds (`cat-file -e`, as task-instance-workspace-phase.yml `Read which of the copy's commits the mirror holds`), pins `<head>` as `refs/orbit/task-base-<instance>` in the mirror, and bundles that ref excluding them; an unpublished `task-42` commit the mirror lacks is never a prerequisite
    %%> In the copy: root makes the bundle folder fresh and owns it; as `agent`, `git fetch` of the bundle into the object store. The publish history reaches the step as a blob
    alt the copy already holds the head
      Note over C: No bundle to fetch<br/>the ref may still be stale
      %%> A copy can hold the pinned commit (an earlier interrupted sync, a merge into task-42) while `refs/remotes/origin/<default>` still names an older commit
    end
    C->>C: Set only the remote ref<br/>update-ref, old value checked
    %%> As `agent`: `git update-ref --no-deref refs/remotes/origin/<default> <head> <old>` with the value read before, refused first when the ref is symbolic, with or without a bundle; no other ref, HEAD, the index, the working tree or stashes is written
    %%> A retry finds the ref already at the head and changes nothing; a ref that moved since the read refuses as `tasks.base_ref_mismatch` rather than overwriting it; any other update failure keeps the ordinary code and its diagnostic
    C-->>EN: Refs and work state<br/>commits · behind_by · work
    %%> The Gateway takes this receipt only when its evidence names the pinned head, the admitted branch and start, and a whole `work` read on that head. Read-back in the same primitive: `refs/remotes/origin/<default>` equals the pinned head, else `tasks.base_ref_mismatch`; HEAD and every local branch equal their values before the step; the branch commit, `git rev-list --count task-42..origin/<default>`, the copy's start and the `work` read (docs/reference/tasks.md#published-work-of-a-copy)
    EN->>N: Clear the base scratch<br/>scratch · pin · bundle folder
    %%> Two steps of one action: `clear` after the import, and `clear_after_failure` after a failed or cancelled fetch or import, as the engine runs no ordinary step after a failure. Each removes `/var/tmp/orbit-task-base-<instance>`, the mirror pin and the copy's bundle folder, and answers only when all three are gone; the import also clears right after its bundle. A later sync or the copy's destroy removes what an interruption left
    N-->>EN: Scratch absent
    opt the receipt is lost
      EN->>C: Resend the same step<br/>fresh nonce · same step ID
      %%> When:
      %%> - the step passes its resend deadline with no receipt; two sends, one execution
      %%> - the Operation keeps its lock, so group 42 and its copy stays fenced; no other Operation and no Swamp run acts on it meanwhile
      %%> On the Node:
      %%> - the journal holds `done` for this Operation step, action and target: the executor answers the stored result with `repeat: true` and does not act again
      %%> - an order still `open` replays under the target lock first; an order that expired before the lock did nothing (`executor.order_expired`), is not journaled as a result, and the step is sent again
      %%> - a result goes back only once its `done` record is durable; content the executor could not read never settles a step
      %%> - the Gateway takes only each step's own evidence: the mirror head, the base evidence or the cleanup; anything else fails the step as `engine.receipt_invalid`
      C-->>EN: Stored result<br/>repeat: true
    end
    alt every step verified
      EN->>GW: Record refs and work<br/>default_commit · behind_by
      %%> - the kind's own projection records the result, the same rows a Swamp run records
    else a step fails
      EN--xGW: Failed step<br/>error_code · redacted detail
      %%> - a deterministic refusal is a terminal receipt too; the journal keeps it and a resend repeats it
      Note over GW: Mark the sync failed<br/>workspace unchanged
      %%> - a cancel sends no new step: it waits for the published order's receipt, clears the scratch and ends cancelled with no field and no error
      %%> - retry: the same command; a new Operation mints a new token, and an earlier fetch makes the next bundle smaller
      %%> - a failed fetch or import leaves the copy's branches and work as they were; only the remote ref may already be newer
    end
  else the engine does not admit it
    Note over GW: Start the Swamp run<br/>operation-task-sync-copy
    %%> - the kind is not enabled, a Node lacks the action, `$KV.NODES` is unreadable, or the flow throws `EngineUnsupported`: the whole Operation runs operation-task-sync-copy (task/sync.mmd)
    %%> - no step of it runs on the engine; an Operation never splits across engines
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
